.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt EMACS-RELEASE-PLAN 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm emacs-release-plan
.Nd plan to release the Emacs distribution 1.0 on 18 December 2026
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
Plan, not started.
EM6 has owner steps that deploy
.Ql docs.example.org
and redirect the old site; it changes a service and DNS.
No step changes a host.
EM6 carries its rollback and checks below.
.Ed
.Pp
The Emacs distribution is the third release of
.Xr jylhis-ship-plan 7 .
The owner uses it each day.
Its largest task is a standalone entry point, which the ledger did not list.
.Ss State on 2026-11-14
.Bl -bullet
.It
Verified: the checks
.Ql emacs-elisp-lint ,
.Ql emacs-module-eval ,
.Ql emacs-docs-ds-in-sync
and
.Ql emacs-docs-build
pass.
.It
Verified on 2026-11-14 (EM4):
.Ql emacs-elisp-test ,
.Ql emacs-elisp-compile
and
.Ql emacs-config-startup
pass.
The cloud container could not download the package sources earlier that day.
Since this page was written,
.Ql just test
runs the ERT suite natively (commit c6ea62497f), and the ERT check writes a
JUnit report (commit b7095b1d8c).
.It
The distribution has a flake (EM2) and no
.Ql package.nix .
It reads
.Ql platform/kit
through
.Ql nix/world.nix ,
which takes the vendored copy in an export, and the design system from the
.Ql jylhis-design
flake input.
The export does not exist yet (EM3).
.It
The licence is set: GPL-3.0-or-later in
.Ql project.nix ,
.Ql LICENSE
and the README; every file under
.Ql lisp/
carries the same GPL-3.0-or-later header (EM8, 2026-11-14).
.It
14 test files cover 35 Lisp files; 47 fragments wait; no version is set.
.It
emacs-overlay is in use, and Emacs 31.1 comes from the binary cache.
.It
.Ql docs.example.org
is not deployed, by TODO.md; the cloud container could not reach the address.
.El
.Ss Selected approach
.Bl -bullet
.It
One flake in the project directory serves the tree and the public repository,
so the two cannot differ.
.It
The design assets and the kit helpers that the distribution uses go into the
export through
.Ql publish.vendor ,
as marchyo does.
.It
The landing page is the existing front page of emacs-docs, with the support
section of the kit.
.El
.Ss Alternatives
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It A synthesized flake
The publish tool can write a flake for a project with a
.Ql package.nix .
The distribution has none and has many inputs, so a written flake is clearer.
.It twist.nix as the build layer
The ledger names it as one option.
emacs-overlay already does that job in the tree, with cache parity, so a
change gives nothing for 1.0.
.El
.Ss Definition of done
.Bl -bullet
.It
The public repository exists under the name of EM1.
.It
.Ql nix flake check
passes in a fresh clone, with no access to jylhis.
.It
.Ql nix run github:Jylhis/<name>
starts Emacs with the configuration.
.It
The installation page describes the Home Manager module and the NixOS module,
and a test evaluates each.
.It
The checks
.Ql emacs-elisp-test ,
.Ql emacs-elisp-compile
and
.Ql emacs-config-startup
pass, with the result on record.
.It
.Ql https://docs.example.org
answers with status 200; the old Pages addresses redirect to it.
.It
The tag
.Ql v1.0.0
exists in the public repository, with a release and its notes.
.It
Each Lisp file has the licence header.
.It
The landing page names the issue tracker, a mail address and the release feed.
.It
.Ql just release-verify emacs
exits with 0.
.El
.Ss Tasks
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It EM1 (owner; 15 minutes; after nothing)
