Correct the platform statement so that it matches
.Ql project.nix .
.It EM6 (sonnet, then owner, then haiku; 1 session, owner 30 minutes, 1 session; after nothing)
The engine cannot bind the domain today.
.Ql projects/services/emacs-docs/project.nix
sets
.Ql deploy.provision = false ,
and
.Ql platform/engines/infra/emitters/workers.nix
then creates no custom domain; the Wrangler configuration declares none.
An infra apply alone leaves
.Ql docs.example.org
without a site.
.Pp
Step 1, agent, idempotent, done on 2026-11-15
.Pq the domain was also bound once through the Cloudflare API, so it answers before the next deploy :
bind the domain in
.Ql wrangler.jsonc
with a route
.Ql { "pattern": "docs.example.org", "custom_domain": true } ,
as the marchyo site does, and correct the comment there that names the engine.
Commit b502bad70e moved the deploy to CI, so the deploy also owns the domain.
The alternative is
.Ql deploy.provision = true ;
it makes the engine create a stub Worker again, which that commit removed.
.Pp
Step 2, owner: confirm the two Cloudflare Actions secrets, and merge so that
the workflow deploys.
No infra apply is necessary for the domain.
.Pp
Step 3, agent: redirect the old GitHub Pages site.
.Pp
Idempotent: the deploy and the redirect are idempotent;
the merge is not, and a second merge is a new commit.
Rollback: before the redirect, remove the route from
.Ql wrangler.jsonc
and deploy again; this removes the custom domain.
After the redirect, revert the redirect commit of the old site.
This restores the old GitHub Pages site as the only address.
No step of EM6 deletes the old site, so this rollback stays possible.
Expected state: the deploy log of the workflow names the custom domain
.Ql docs.example.org ;
the old address answers with a redirect.
Check: run
.Ql curl -sI https://docs.example.org
and expect a status 200, and run
.Ql curl -sI
on the old address and expect a status 301.
No command of this step ran for this plan; all are unverified.
.Pp
Known effects:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
DNS takes minutes to propagate; the site can answer 404 or a certificate error in that time.
.It
Visitors of the old address land on the new landing page; old deep links can fail.
.It
Each push to green main starts a Workers Builds run (free tier).
.El
